{
  "title": "Diastrophic Dysplasia",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4097/diastrophic-dysplasia",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 17 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Diastrophic Dysplasia is a rare congenital disorder caused by an autosomal recessive mutation in the DTDST gene leading to a defect in the sulfate transporter protein. Patients present with a form of short-limbed dwarfism with characteristic features such as cauliflower ears, hitchhiker thumbs, and severe cervical kyphosis.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made based on family history associated with typical radiographic and clinical features. No commercially available diagnostic test exists due to the variety of genetic mutations.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment involves a multidisciplinary approach to improve and maintain function. Surgical spinal instrumentation and fusion are indicated in patients with atlantoaxial instability, cervical myelopathy, or progressive scoliosis.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "more common in **Finland**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "rare in rest of world",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Genetics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**autosomal recessive**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "mutation in **DTDST gene** (SLC26A2) on chromosome 5",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "encodes for **sulfate transporter protein**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**mutation is present in 1 in 70 Finnish citizens**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "leads to undersulfation of cartilage proteoglycan",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Physical exam and syndrome features",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "short stature (\"**twisted dwarf**\")",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "rhizomelic shortening",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "cleft palate (60%)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**cauliflower ears (80%)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4097/images/cauliflower%20ear%20-%20colorado_moved.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "poorly developed UE",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**hitchhikers thumb**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4097/images/hitchhikers%20thumb%20-%20colorado_moved.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "thoracolumbar scoliosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**severe cervical kyphosis**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4097/images/Cervical%20kyphosis_moved.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "hip and knee contractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**genu valgum**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**skewfoot (serpentine or Z foot)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "tarsometatarsal adductus and valgus hindfoot",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**rigid clubfeet (equinocavovarus)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4097/images/Clubfeet_moved.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP and lateral of cervical spine and thoracolumbar spine",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "three joint standing lower extremity films to assess alignment",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ultrasound",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "can be used to make diagnosis prenatally",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "observation and supportive treatment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "most patients",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**modalities**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**cauliflower ears** frequently repsond to early treatment with **compressive bandages**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "cervical kyphosis frequently resolves spontaneously",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "occipital-cervical fusion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "atlantoaxial instability with neurologic symptoms",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "risk of quadriplegia is a concern",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "posterior cervical fusion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "cervical kyphosis that does not resolve spontaneously",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "thoracolumbar fusion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "kyphoscoliosis of thoracolumbar spine",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "if progressive may require ASF / PSF",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "soft tissue surgical release",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "early foot ankle deformity after initial period of casting",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "severe joint contractures (hip and knee)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "osteotomies for correction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "progressive **valgus deformity** of lower extremities (with dislocated patellae)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "resistant or recurrent clubfeet",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "distal femoral extension osteotomies for fixed knee flexion contractures",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "valgus intertrochanteric osteotomies +/- acetabuloplasty for early hip subluxation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "total joint arthroplasty",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "end stage osteoarthritis of hips",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
